# Default stack
- Backend: ASP.NET Core modular monolith. Database: PostgreSQL (PostGIS only when geo matters). Redis for cache/session/rate-limit. Queue for heavy work. Object storage for files.
- Web: Next.js. Mobile, if any: React Native (Expo) or Flutter, with a versioned API. One backend language per product.
- Do not default to MySQL, PHP, NestJS, microservices, or CQRS. SQL Server only with an explicit Azure lock-in.
- Small apps stay thin: few projects, EF Core.
